 "notes": "Second read of strip b. Names as printed: APPLE, DHONAU, SPRING GROVE AVE., FORD ST., ARCHIBALD ST., LUDLOW AVE., STRENG, OBANNION (no apostrophe), KELLY LANE, TOP ST., ERHARDT ST., COLERAIN, RALSTON AVE. 60', WHITLEY ST., ELMIRA AVE., BRASHEARS ST., ADELAIDE ST., PRIMROSE ST., ARLINGTON ST., SASSAFRAS, JOHNSON, LEOLIE ST. Powers, Burgoyne ('ST' only here) and Elmore names come from 37L / the old file. 'E. KNOWLTON'S', 'GRANTWOODFORK', 'C.E. WILLIAMS PER SH'FF', 'J.C. BRUCKMAN'S', 'CLIFTON FARM', 'JOHN WATSON'S HEIRS LOTS' are tract names, not streets; the orange/pink, gray, blue and green bands are tract or dedication lines (the gray strip along Colerain's west side and Streng is labelled as dedicated to the City of Cincinnati for street). Not picked (unnamed): the two 'NO NAME' streets SE of Archibald; the unnamed stub at the top edge crossing Mill Creek to Ludlow (~2450,150); a ~20 ft alley east of Ford at y ~1570; a narrow passage at x ~1990 from Streng to Erhardt (letter 'H' printed in it, probably a tract letter); the street printed only 'ROAD' that starts at the canal bed (~2710,5370) and runs east (it does not reach Colerain). Railroads (B&O S.W., the spur at x ~1960 crossing Primrose/Arlington/Sassafras, the line through block 72) not picked. Spring Grove's corridor is wide (~165 px incl. tracks); its centre was taken midway between the block lines."
